Design and build a complete desktop-first and mobile-responsive website concept in Figma Make for a premium curated marketplace brand called CULTE.

IMPORTANT BRAND RULES
- Follow the attached brand booklet exactly in spirit and system.
- Background must be pure white across the website.
- Brand feel: premium, cool, bold, contemporary, curated, editorial, product-first.
- Typography:
  - Use Valibuk for brand logotype, major headings, navigation labels, category labels, CTA labels.
  - Use Poppins Medium / Regular for body copy, product titles, descriptions, UI text, pricing, form labels.
- Color palette:
  - White #FFFFFF as the main website ground always.
  - Deep Navy #181E51 for navigation, headers, key anchors.
  - Burnt Orange #E17544 for CTA, highlights, active states. Use orange only once per surface.
  - Light Blue #C2DFED for cards, soft image backgrounds, empty states, hover fills, secondary sections.
  - Soft Peach #F19D73 for selected editorial moments only.
  - Near-black #0F0F0F only for body text, never for logo/brand expression.
- Overall visual direction:
  - White-background marketplace
  - Bold CULTE. logo in nav
  - Open spacing
  - Premium concept-store feeling
  - Easy to use, innovative but not experimental to the point of confusion
  - No dark theme, no beige ground, no clutter, no generic marketplace look

PROJECT GOAL
Create a full marketplace website UX/UI system for CULTE where:
- buyers can browse and buy products
- buyers can sign up and log in
- sellers can log in through a dedicated seller portal
- sellers can upload and manage products through a seller dashboard
- products are organized through clear category structures
- all components are fully designed and reusable
- all page links and flows are complete and connected
- all buttons, cards, fields, tabs, filters, nav items, badges, modals, and states are created as downloadable components
- all pages should feel like one premium design system, not random screens

