REQUIRED UX STRUCTURE
This must be a real marketplace, not just a homepage mockup.

A. Homepage
Design a premium homepage with:
- bold hero section
- curated category shortcuts
- “The Edit” editorial section
- featured brands / sellers
- new arrivals product grid
- trending categories
- a premium marketplace trust section
- CTA areas for both shopping and seller application/login
- newsletter/footer section
The homepage should feel editorial and commercial at the same time.

B. Category Structure
Include clear category navigation and landing pages.
Create example top-level categories such as:
- Women
- Men
- Home
- Beauty
- Objects
- Kids
Also include subcategory filtering logic.
Every category page should include:
- title banner
- filter sidebar or top filter row
- sorting
- breadcrumbs
- product count
- product cards
- pagination or load more
- filter chips
- active/inactive states

C. Product Detail Page
Include:
- large product media gallery
- product title
- price
- seller / brand name
- category breadcrumb
- variation selectors if needed
- add to bag
- save / wishlist
- delivery info
- description
- specifications
- shipping / returns
- related products
- more from this seller
- trust indicators
- mobile sticky CTA

D. Seller Dashboard
This is essential.
Create a dedicated seller dashboard with clean UX and premium UI.
Must include:
- overview cards
- analytics snapshot
- add new product CTA
- product upload flow
- product table
- inventory status
- order management
- payout summary
- account and store settings
- support/help panel
Design product upload as a clean multi-step form:
- product name
- description
- price
- category
- subcategory
- tags
- SKU
- stock
- media upload
- shipping info
- save draft / publish
The seller experience should be simple and frictionless.

E. Buyer Login and Seller Login
Create separate login entry points:
- buyer login / sign up
- seller login
Do not merge them into one confusing screen.
The seller login should feel slightly more operational but still on-brand.

